1
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,679
She thinks I killed Claire?

2
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:15,719
<i>Maybe it's better this way.</i>

3
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:17,599
<i>So she'll stay alert.</i>

4
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:20,040
Mr. Thiwa implied
leaving everything to Claire.

5
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:24,519
<i>I don't know if he was testing me.</i>

6
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:26,679
I'm not taking even a 1% chance.

7
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:30,439
I'm Ms. Claire, Vice Chairman of TGL.

8
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:34,040
<i>But no matter what,
you're not the real Ms. Claire.</i>

9
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:36,000
<i>From now on,</i>

10
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:39,840
<i>I'm gonna be Claire in my own way.</i>

11
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:47,000
MOBILE
SLIDE TO ANSWER

12
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:57,839
What's up?

13
00:00:57,840 --> 00:00:59,400
I won't go in today.

14
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:03,240
Ms. Claire called a team meeting?

15
00:01:04,840 --> 00:01:05,880
I'm on my way.

16
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:25,280
Ms. Claire, they're ready for you.

17
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:27,640
Okay, I'll be right there.

18
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:33,640
Okay.

19
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:37,080
I can do this.

20
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:44,400
Claire.

21
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:48,920
I've been told you came in today.

22
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:51,399
We haven't talked lately, Claire.

23
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:53,200
Hey, what are you doing?

24
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:56,720
Are you mad at me?

25
00:01:57,960 --> 00:02:01,559
Because I didn't protect you
at the vault room? I can explain, Claire.

26
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:03,119
Why do you have to explain?

27
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:05,239
What you did was the right thing.

28
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:08,600
The person you should protect is Cha,
not me.

29
00:02:10,199 --> 00:02:12,120
- Claire.
- Hey, stop.

30
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:14,160
Just leave me alone.

31
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:17,319
If you won't stop, I'll have to fire you.

32
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:19,679
And if Cha asks for a reason,

33
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:21,879
I'll have to tell her the truth

34
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:24,600
that I don't want an asshole
like you working here.

35
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:27,640
Then I'll tell her to stay away from you.

36
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:38,160
You're dumping me, bitch?

37
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:45,679
And I want us to hold two events
before the anniversary.

38
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:49,280
What about celebrities?
Do you want anyone in particular?

39
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:51,639
No.

40
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:53,519
I'd rather work with influencers.

41
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:57,280
Find me the top three influencers
on each platform and I'll choose.

42
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:58,840
Got it.

43
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,719
Okay, that's all for today.

44
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:16,319
I want the script by 4 p.m.,
so please get on it.

45
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:17,880
Yes, Ms. Claire.

46
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:35,160
What are you trying to do?

47
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:40,719
I'm planning the promotion
for our 60th anniversary.

48
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:44,120
It's a major event.
I want it to be as perfect as possible.

49
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:54,119
Excuse me, Ms. Claire.

50
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:57,039
Ms. Ooh called back.
She rearranged the schedule.

51
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:59,559
You can go to the studio tomorrow.

52
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:00,800
Okay.

53
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:05,160
Hey.

54
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:06,680
Who is Ms. Ooh?

55
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:10,519
And why are you going to a studio?
Why haven't I been informed?

56
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:12,880
I'm going on <i>Wonderful Tonight</i> tomorrow.

57
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,000
Wait.

58
00:04:17,839 --> 00:04:20,040
What are you trying to do, huh?

59
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:22,920
I'm just doing what I should be doing.

60
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,479
You heard the chairman last night.

61
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:28,279
He's looking forward to
what we came up with.

62
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:29,960
I don't want to disappoint him.

63
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:34,520
Ow. Hey.

64
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:39,560
Ow. Hey!

65
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:42,359
Hey.

66
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:43,639
What's gotten into you?

67
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:45,440
What are you up to?

68
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:48,199
I already answered you.

69
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:51,999
I'm not your secretary.
It's not my job to brief you on meetings.

70
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,719
You know what I'm talking about.

71
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:56,359
Yesterday you said
you didn't want to work here.

72
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:59,240
And now what?
You're calling a team meeting?

73
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:00,880
Huh?

74
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:03,040
Have you lost your mind?

75
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:05,720
Why not?

76
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:11,000
Is it so crazy for a CEO
to call a meeting and assign work?

77
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:15,760
You're a CEO?

78
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,320
What right do you have?

79
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,439
I have every right.

80
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:21,999
Because I'm Claire.

81
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,839
You should be happy.

82
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:26,520
I'm finally trying
to become Claire for real.

83
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,039
Even if it's not in the way you like.

84
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:31,360
Because I'm gonna be Claire in my own way.

85
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:37,320
You're gonna be Claire in your own way?

86
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,040
You're well aware.

87
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:47,920
No matter how hard I try,
I can never become the real Ms. Claire.

88
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:53,280
So from now on,
I'm gonna be Claire as myself.

89
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:58,920
And you think I'll let you do that?

90
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:03,920
Why don't we find out?

91
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:07,480
Let's see what this puppet can really do.

92
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,559
Ms. Claire called a meeting
to promote the anniversary?

93
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:56,079
Yes, she did.

94
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:58,519
She asked us to come up with
two or three events.

95
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:00,839
And submit everything by this week.

96
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:04,079
But I don't know if her appearance
on Mr. Wonder's show tomorrow

97
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:06,840
is part of the promotion plan.

98
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:09,520
Mr. Wonder's show?

99
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:12,320
But it's not easy to get on that show.

100
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:17,160
It's not. They said yes right away
once they heard it was Ms. Claire.

101
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:22,439
Okay, that's all we wanted to know.

102
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:23,400
You can go.

103
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,080
Okay.

104
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:33,079
Something feels off.

105
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:35,520
Why is Claire suddenly doing all this?

106
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:39,400
Why? Worried about her?

107
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:42,999
Cha, will you drop it?

108
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,240
You know it's nothing.

109
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:51,000
I'm just curious as to what she's up to.

110
00:08:52,520 --> 00:08:53,760
What else could it be?

111
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:56,640
She just wants to impress my dad.

112
00:08:58,160 --> 00:08:59,679
And what are you doing about it?

113
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:02,280
You're just letting
her steal the spotlight?

114
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:06,559
I'm excited to see

115
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:09,760
if an amnesiac going on TV

116
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:14,000
will earn praise or embarrass herself.

117
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:25,959
Hello, Pong. I'm almost there.

118
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:28,480
I'm sorry. Something unexpected came up.

119
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,080
What?

120
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:37,120
I don't have to come anymore?

121
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:42,160
It's totally okay if you're busy.
You can have someone else interview me.

122
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:46,240
Really?

123
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:51,320
Okay.

124
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:54,920
Wait, Pong.

125
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:56,960
Did...

126
00:09:58,120 --> 00:10:01,520
did I lose the job because of my scandal?

127
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:03,720
I see.

128
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:06,760
Yeah, but...

129
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:15,960
People make mistakes. What else can I do?

130
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:18,959
Whatever.

131
00:10:18,960 --> 00:10:20,480
This won't kill me.

132
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:23,280
Any jobs out there for me?

133
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:35,280
It's me.

134
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:37,640
You?

135
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,640
Hello, Ms. Wan.

136
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:49,040
What now? Did Ms. Claire
send you to mess with me again?

137
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:52,080
Not at all.

138
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:54,960
Ms. Claire wants you to work with us.

139
00:10:56,240 --> 00:10:59,800
Ms. Claire wants me to work for her?

140
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:01,999
Yes.

141
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,400
<i>Take me to the office.</i>

142
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:05,280
To do what, ma'am?

143
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:07,600
To be Ms. Claire.

144
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:10,159
What do you mean?

145
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:14,079
I couldn't hire Wan
because I'm not Ms. Claire.

146
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:16,400
To help her, I have to be Ms. Claire.

147
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:20,200
I may not understand your goal here,

148
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:24,560
but if you want to go to the office,
I have to call Chan.

149
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,440
No.

150
00:11:27,640 --> 00:11:31,680
If you don't want me telling people
what you two did to me, don't call him.

151
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:36,399
Take me to the office.

152
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:37,799
Then go see Wan.

153
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:39,760
Do whatever it takes to get a yes.

154
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:44,039
I can tell her what you want me to say,

155
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:49,040
but you know very well
she'd never agree to work with us.

156
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:55,440
Then you should already know my answer.

157
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:59,119
Even if no one else will hire me,

158
00:11:59,120 --> 00:12:01,319
I'll never work for Ms. Claire.

159
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:02,239
Excuse me.

160
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:03,920
Wait a second.

161
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:07,240
Sorry.

162
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:08,920
I forgot this.

163
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:27,320
<i>After this job's over,
I'll take you to see the penguins.</i>

164
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:33,239
If I win this award next year,

165
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:35,960
I'll take you to see the penguins.

166
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:39,720
This is Jin's handwriting.

167
00:12:40,520 --> 00:12:41,760
How did you get this?

168
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:44,720
It's from Ms. Claire.

169
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:48,680
As for how she got this message
from Ms. Jin,

170
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:50,960
she'll tell you herself.

171
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:48,839
Most of these questions are good,

172
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:52,480
but I'd like to limit questions
about the 60th anniversary.

173
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:55,320
I want Mr. Wonder to focus on the crash.

174
00:13:58,320 --> 00:13:59,639
What's wrong?

175
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:04,199
Well, Mr. Chan previously
instructed the PR team

176
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:07,560
to avoid talking about your crash.

177
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:11,360
Secrets get people curious.

178
00:14:12,160 --> 00:14:13,280
Just do as I said.

179
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:37,239
Looks like
Ms. Wan recognized your handwriting.

180
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:40,320
Really? And what did she say?

181
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:42,800
She said no.

182
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:48,480
It must've thrown her off.

183
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:51,600
That's okay. Let's give her some time.

184
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:59,159
If you're here
about the interview questions,

185
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:01,440
- let me tell you--
- This is Claire's phone.

186
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:04,000
You should use it.

187
00:15:06,520 --> 00:15:07,600
Wait.

188
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:10,520
You're allowing me to use a phone?

189
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:13,920
I just had the data recovered.

190
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:16,480
You can use it.

191
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:21,919
Are you not worried I'll tell people
that I'm not Ms. Claire?

192
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:24,119
You would've done that a long time ago.

193
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:25,959
Besides,

194
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:28,120
didn't you just say

195
00:15:28,680 --> 00:15:31,240
you're going to be Claire in your own way?

196
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:34,480
So you won't tell anyone.

197
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:40,640
I'm not done.

198
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:42,879
I'm allowing you to use it,

199
00:15:42,880 --> 00:15:45,839
but only under Claire's account.

200
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:48,240
Do not log in with any other account.

201
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:50,720
I know that.

202
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:09,760
I'm glad you gave her Ms. Claire's phone.

203
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:14,200
Someone else might call to congratulate
Ms. Claire for surviving.

204
00:16:14,880 --> 00:16:18,520
And if her phone stays off,
that'll make things suspicious.

205
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:27,200
Chan, are you okay?

206
00:16:32,520 --> 00:16:34,919
Someone called from a hidden number

207
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:37,360
when I turned Claire's phone back on.

208
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:40,599
And...

209
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:42,320
And you didn't answer, right?

210
00:16:44,360 --> 00:16:48,040
This person doesn't want us
to know who they are.

211
00:16:49,640 --> 00:16:53,760
And if I'd answered,
they may never contact Claire again.

212
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:57,240
So you're thinking...

213
00:16:58,120 --> 00:17:00,400
the caller is connected to the crash.

214
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:04,400
That's why you gave her
Ms. Claire's phone, isn't it?

215
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:11,880
You're using her as bait
to make them call again.

216
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:25,040
I know doing this puts her in danger.

217
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:32,360
But we have to take the risk.

218
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:35,800
Because I think they may be
connected to Claire's death.

219
00:17:58,600 --> 00:18:00,400
Why aren't there more pictures?

220
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:11,879
SELECTED EIGHT PHOTOS

221
00:18:11,880 --> 00:18:13,480
DELETE EIGHT PHOTOS CANCEL

222
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:19,680
<i>Ms. Claire,</i>

223
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:24,360
<i>let me tell you,
our lives couldn't be more different.</i>

224
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:26,320
<i>We have nothing in common.</i>

225
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:28,959
<i>But it's funny.</i>

226
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:31,399
<i>No matter how different our lives were,</i>

227
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:34,400
<i>we ended up with the same fate.</i>

228
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:38,600
<i>No.</i>

229
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,520
<i>My life isn't over yet.</i>

230
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:59,040
Look up the private number
that called Claire's phone.

231
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:02,680
You have the number, right?

232
00:19:05,760 --> 00:19:07,520
I need it ASAP.

233
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:20,479
<i>Hi, everyone. It's me, Claire.</i>

234
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:22,119
<i>Khaedarun Kanchathara.</i>

235
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:24,359
<i>I'll be on Wonder's show tomorrow.</i>

236
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:26,759
<i>I've got so much I want to share.</i>

237
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:29,239
Hey, look at this.

238
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:30,800
Let me see.

239
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:34,160
I bet Ms. Claire's faking amnesia.

240
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:36,880
Or she wouldn't go on Wonder's show.

241
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:40,239
Yeah, sounds about right.

242
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:43,440
She's just got back
and she's already making headlines.

243
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:46,360
Do you think it's possible?

244
00:19:47,040 --> 00:19:49,520
It's probably what it says.

245
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:24,159
UNBELIEVABLE. CAN'T WAIT.

246
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:27,199
IF SURVIVING MAKES ME PRETTIER,
I'LL KILL MYSELF TEN TIMES.

247
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:28,999
LOOKING FORWARD TO IT. CAN'T WAIT.

248
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:32,440
CAN'T WAIT FOR MS. CLAIRE'S EPISODE.
ALWAYS WANTED HER ON THIS SHOW.

249
00:20:41,840 --> 00:20:43,159
<i>Just wait.</i>

250
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:45,520
<i>Tomorrow everyone's going to meet
a brand-new Claire.</i>

251
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:50,280
Hey?

252
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:52,800
Hey?

253
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:54,640
I'm coming in.

254
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:24,000
Hey!

255
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:25,400
Hey!

256
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:30,559
Hey!

257
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:32,400
Are you okay? Hey.

258
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:34,320
Hey.

259
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:40,520
Hey! What are you doing?

260
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:43,600
I didn't mean to.

261
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:47,119
What are you doing? Get out! Go!

262
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:49,600
Okay, I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

263
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:18,320
I was just...

264
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:20,119
picking out clothes.

265
00:22:20,120 --> 00:22:22,680
I didn't see anything I liked,
so it took a while.

266
00:22:23,280 --> 00:22:24,360
Wasn't because of you.

267
00:22:25,040 --> 00:22:26,519
But I knocked first.

268
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:29,239
And I called you really loud.
You didn't answer. I got worried,

269
00:22:29,240 --> 00:22:31,399
- so came in...
- That's enough, I get it.

270
00:22:31,400 --> 00:22:32,760
No need to elaborate.

271
00:22:34,080 --> 00:22:35,520
Why did you come in here?

272
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:39,720
I just read...

273
00:22:40,320 --> 00:22:42,559
the script for tomorrow's show.

274
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:45,839
So I thought I'd help you rehearse.

275
00:22:45,840 --> 00:22:50,120
I already told you that
I'm going to be Claire in my own way.

276
00:22:50,760 --> 00:22:54,640
So I'm gonna answer in a way
that shows people who I really am.

277
00:22:57,280 --> 00:23:00,280
But the script is missing one thing.

278
00:23:02,120 --> 00:23:03,000
What's that?

279
00:23:04,200 --> 00:23:05,280
Me, of course.

280
00:23:06,920 --> 00:23:10,759
You know these variety talk shows

281
00:23:10,760 --> 00:23:14,239
love to get into people's personal life.

282
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:17,320
And most importantly,
they love getting into romance.

283
00:23:20,840 --> 00:23:22,039
Don't worry.

284
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:25,320
I told Wonder not to ask anything
beyond what I briefed him on.

285
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,680
And if he does ask, what will you do?

286
00:23:32,360 --> 00:23:33,400
What?

287
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:41,360
I want the two of us
to try showing some affection.

288
00:23:52,920 --> 00:23:54,639
Hey, wait.

289
00:23:54,640 --> 00:23:56,320
What are you doing?

290
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:09,080
How do you feel about me?

291
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:31,320
Let's try that again.

292
00:24:34,840 --> 00:24:39,400
What you just did showed everyone
we're not really engaged.

293
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:41,440
What do you mean?

294
00:24:42,520 --> 00:24:43,599
Hey.

295
00:24:43,600 --> 00:24:45,359
Think about it.

296
00:24:45,360 --> 00:24:48,679
Would people in love look terrified
and squeeze their eyes shut

297
00:24:48,680 --> 00:24:50,520
when their partner tries to kiss them?

298
00:24:51,440 --> 00:24:53,319
Let's try rehearsing that again.

299
00:24:53,320 --> 00:24:54,559
Come on. Come here.

300
00:24:54,560 --> 00:24:55,480
No.

301
00:24:57,360 --> 00:24:59,799
It won't work
even if we rehearse all night.

302
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:01,239
You know why?

303
00:25:01,240 --> 00:25:03,440
Because we're not in love.

304
00:25:04,520 --> 00:25:08,599
And you don't need to worry.
I'll tell Wonder not to ask about this.

305
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:10,159
Now you can relax.

306
00:25:10,160 --> 00:25:11,959
Anything else?

307
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:14,439
If that's all, you should leave.

308
00:25:14,440 --> 00:25:16,400
I'm sleepy. Come on.

309
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:20,600
Please.

310
00:25:22,480 --> 00:25:23,759
Hey.

311
00:25:23,760 --> 00:25:27,800
Don't tell me you've changed
your mind and want to rehearse.

312
00:25:29,640 --> 00:25:31,239
I was gonna tell you

313
00:25:31,240 --> 00:25:33,480
you don't have to come with me tomorrow.

314
00:25:34,120 --> 00:25:37,239
If they don't see you,
they probably won't ask about us.

315
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:38,399
I'll go with Tun.

316
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:39,960
Okay? Go.

317
00:26:05,480 --> 00:26:06,520
Hey.

318
00:26:07,120 --> 00:26:08,280
You can't, Jinla.

319
00:26:09,160 --> 00:26:11,080
You need to focus on tomorrow.

320
00:26:12,880 --> 00:26:13,960
No.

321
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:23,760
- Ms. Claire, hello.
- Hello.

322
00:26:25,360 --> 00:26:26,880
You seem familiar with this place.

323
00:26:29,680 --> 00:26:31,759
I used to be Wonder's creative producer.

324
00:26:31,760 --> 00:26:33,159
Oh, Ms. Claire!

325
00:26:33,160 --> 00:26:35,159
Hello, Ms. Claire.

326
00:26:35,160 --> 00:26:37,519
Why are you here so early?

327
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:41,599
I'm free this morning,
so I thought I'd come wait here.

328
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:43,759
Better to wait than keep others waiting.

329
00:26:43,760 --> 00:26:46,320
That's why you're the best, Ms. Claire.

330
00:26:47,040 --> 00:26:48,360
That's just who she is.

331
00:27:00,040 --> 00:27:03,240
She loves surprising people. Right?

332
00:27:04,640 --> 00:27:07,120
Not as much as you like surprising me.

333
00:27:10,840 --> 00:27:13,159
Chan said he couldn't make it today.

334
00:27:13,160 --> 00:27:15,400
Said he was tied up with work, Wonder.

335
00:27:17,600 --> 00:27:19,279
Of course I had to come.

336
00:27:19,280 --> 00:27:21,279
My fiancée is filming today.

337
00:27:21,280 --> 00:27:23,439
I had to come cheer her on.

338
00:27:23,440 --> 00:27:24,440
Right?

339
00:27:26,440 --> 00:27:29,319
Mr. Chan seems to care about you
a lot, Ms. Claire.

340
00:27:29,320 --> 00:27:33,240
He even walked around to check
that everything was in order.

341
00:27:34,600 --> 00:27:36,919
Ms. Claire, please wait here for a moment.

342
00:27:36,920 --> 00:27:39,119
I'll have someone take you to the lounge.

343
00:27:39,120 --> 00:27:40,359
- Okay.
- Just a moment.

344
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:41,360
Sure.

345
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:47,999
What are you doing?

346
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:50,160
I told you not to come.

347
00:27:51,440 --> 00:27:52,880
I just wanted to see...

348
00:27:54,400 --> 00:27:57,080
what being Claire
in your own way looks like.

349
00:28:00,080 --> 00:28:01,680
Then just wait and see.

350
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:12,319
Ms. Claire, come sit over here.

351
00:28:12,320 --> 00:28:13,560
Okay.

352
00:28:14,720 --> 00:28:17,120
Have a seat.
Would you like something to drink?

353
00:28:17,880 --> 00:28:19,639
Just water is fine.

354
00:28:19,640 --> 00:28:20,719
Hey, bring some water.

355
00:28:20,720 --> 00:28:23,200
<i>Have you seen her IG story
on Ms. Claire's account? What now?</i>

356
00:28:24,080 --> 00:28:27,800
Tomorrow we might find out
who killed Claire.

357
00:28:29,480 --> 00:28:31,320
Remember her shellfish allergy attack?

358
00:28:33,760 --> 00:28:35,160
Why? What about it?

359
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:38,800
It was her first media appearance.

360
00:28:45,200 --> 00:28:48,799
Hello and welcome to <i>Wonderful Show.</i>

361
00:28:48,800 --> 00:28:52,359
I'm so happy to interview
this woman today.

362
00:28:52,360 --> 00:28:53,439
She recently went through

363
00:28:53,440 --> 00:28:57,599
a near-death experience
in a helicopter crash.

364
00:28:57,600 --> 00:29:02,920
Please welcome Ms. Khaedarun Kanchathara!

365
00:29:06,640 --> 00:29:10,280
<i>By now everyone knows
Claire's out of the hospital.</i>

366
00:29:10,920 --> 00:29:12,599
<i>Think about it.</i>

367
00:29:12,600 --> 00:29:17,120
<i>If the person who tried to kill Claire
catches the news, what'll they do?</i>

368
00:29:17,760 --> 00:29:20,719
<i>They'll be shocked seeing her still alive.</i>

369
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:23,160
<i>And they'll look for
another chance to strike.</i>

370
00:29:41,560 --> 00:29:44,759
Even though this is
your first time on the show,

371
00:29:44,760 --> 00:29:47,079
I'd like to say this.

372
00:29:47,080 --> 00:29:49,359
Welcome back.

373
00:29:49,360 --> 00:29:53,839
<i>Do you know what I am referring to?</i>

374
00:29:53,840 --> 00:29:56,960
<i>I do. I'm happy to be back too.</i>

375
00:29:57,560 --> 00:29:59,680
<i>Are you still shaken up?</i>

376
00:30:00,280 --> 00:30:01,359
I'm better now.

377
00:30:01,360 --> 00:30:04,919
But I still wake up startled
sometimes at night.

378
00:30:04,920 --> 00:30:08,839
I think a lot of people
want to know about this.

379
00:30:08,840 --> 00:30:11,199
When the helicopter was going down,

380
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:13,639
what was going through your mind?

381
00:30:13,640 --> 00:30:15,440
Were you scared? Things like that.

382
00:30:16,080 --> 00:30:18,759
I'm totally okay talking about it.

383
00:30:18,760 --> 00:30:22,839
<i>Actually, the reason I came
on the show was to discuss it.</i>

384
00:30:22,840 --> 00:30:28,279
Very few people survive
an accident that serious the way I did.

385
00:30:28,280 --> 00:30:30,799
<i>Wow, the way you're talking about it</i>

386
00:30:30,800 --> 00:30:32,799
has really got me curious.

387
00:30:32,800 --> 00:30:35,639
But today there's someone else

388
00:30:35,640 --> 00:30:38,879
who wanted to hear you
tell your story in person.

389
00:30:38,880 --> 00:30:41,480
MS. KHAEDARUN OPENS UP
AFTER SURVIVING A NEAR-DEATH EXPERIENCE

390
00:30:56,600 --> 00:30:58,359
Whoa, sir. Why are you following me?

391
00:30:58,360 --> 00:31:00,559
- Why are you here?
- I'm making a delivery.

392
00:31:00,560 --> 00:31:02,279
- Delivering what?
- I have no idea.

393
00:31:02,280 --> 00:31:04,519
I'm just here to drop it off. Whoa, sir!

394
00:31:04,520 --> 00:31:05,799
Open the case.

395
00:31:05,800 --> 00:31:08,679
What the hell? I can't.
It's a customer's case.

396
00:31:08,680 --> 00:31:09,639
What the hell, sir?

397
00:31:09,640 --> 00:31:10,959
Who sent you?

398
00:31:10,960 --> 00:31:12,599
No one, sir. I'm a delivery man.

399
00:31:12,600 --> 00:31:13,719
Who sent you?!

400
00:31:13,720 --> 00:31:15,519
Ow! No one, sir

401
00:31:15,520 --> 00:31:16,479
Who sent you?

402
00:31:16,480 --> 00:31:17,719
No one!

403
00:31:17,720 --> 00:31:18,879
What's going on?

404
00:31:18,880 --> 00:31:20,599
Are you here for a delivery?

405
00:31:20,600 --> 00:31:22,519
Yes. Please calm down.

406
00:31:22,520 --> 00:31:24,160
It's really a delivery.

407
00:31:24,880 --> 00:31:25,840
See?

408
00:31:26,800 --> 00:31:28,480
Here, it's cosmetics.

409
00:31:30,360 --> 00:31:34,080
Please welcome Ms. Cha
with a round of applause!

410
00:31:46,120 --> 00:31:48,439
After Ms. Claire approves the questions,

411
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:50,080
keep working on your prep.

412
00:31:50,880 --> 00:31:53,840
You know how demanding
Ms. Claire can be, right?

413
00:31:54,560 --> 00:31:58,800
Oh my gosh. If we don't crash and burn
tomorrow, our company will be famous.

414
00:32:00,120 --> 00:32:01,559
I'm serious.

415
00:32:01,560 --> 00:32:03,759
No mistakes tomorrow.

416
00:32:03,760 --> 00:32:06,599
You're excited too, huh?
Okay, see you tomorrow.

417
00:32:06,600 --> 00:32:07,720
Bye.

418
00:32:10,680 --> 00:32:11,759
Oops.

419
00:32:11,760 --> 00:32:15,920
Oh, Ms. Cha, what brings you here?

420
00:32:16,800 --> 00:32:18,440
I came to see you

421
00:32:19,080 --> 00:32:20,080
That's right.

422
00:32:20,840 --> 00:32:22,599
I'll get right to the point.

423
00:32:22,600 --> 00:32:26,440
I want to surprise Claire
on your show tomorrow.

424
00:32:27,160 --> 00:32:31,159
Well, Ms. Claire already
approved the questions.

425
00:32:31,160 --> 00:32:36,200
But if you want to surprise her,
let me inform her first.

426
00:32:37,480 --> 00:32:39,480
Do you not understand what a surprise is?

427
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:47,000
I get it if you're worried
about the fight Claire and I had.

428
00:32:47,760 --> 00:32:49,639
But if you think about it,

429
00:32:49,640 --> 00:32:51,599
this could actually help the show.

430
00:32:51,600 --> 00:32:53,880
The ratings would be great too.

431
00:32:54,680 --> 00:32:55,919
Well...

432
00:32:55,920 --> 00:32:58,279
Or if you're still hesitant,

433
00:32:58,280 --> 00:33:00,799
should I switch to another story?

434
00:33:00,800 --> 00:33:04,719
About a male host
who paid for sex with a minor,

435
00:33:04,720 --> 00:33:08,120
then did drugs with them
at his condo in Thonglor.

436
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:12,520
A friend of mine lives in that condo too.

437
00:33:13,120 --> 00:33:14,519
So?

438
00:33:14,520 --> 00:33:16,399
Will you let me surprise Claire?

439
00:33:16,400 --> 00:33:18,680
Or should I call a reporter right now?

440
00:33:29,800 --> 00:33:32,560
- Hello, Ms. Cha. Please have a seat.
- Hello.

441
00:33:33,320 --> 00:33:35,559
<i>Ms. Claire, I hope you don't mind</i>

442
00:33:35,560 --> 00:33:39,000
<i>that I invited Ms. Cha to join us
and congratulate you.</i>

443
00:33:39,680 --> 00:33:41,879
<i>Oh, not at all.</i>

444
00:33:41,880 --> 00:33:44,679
I was just surprised.
I didn't expect it to be Cha.

445
00:33:44,680 --> 00:33:47,160
Because we see each other
almost every day.

446
00:33:47,880 --> 00:33:50,319
Yes, it's true we see
each other almost every day,

447
00:33:50,320 --> 00:33:52,959
but we both come from a business family.

448
00:33:52,960 --> 00:33:57,480
We're so busy with work that we hardly
have time for personal conversations.

449
00:33:58,080 --> 00:34:01,599
But when I heard Claire was
coming on your show today,

450
00:34:01,600 --> 00:34:03,039
<i>I cleared my schedule right away.</i>

451
00:34:03,040 --> 00:34:07,720
<i>Because I wanted to represent
our family and congratulate her.</i>

452
00:34:08,320 --> 00:34:10,199
<i>On surviving the helicopter crash.</i>

453
00:34:16,840 --> 00:34:17,679
There you are.

454
00:34:19,400 --> 00:34:21,599
Aren't you watching Claire's interview?

455
00:34:21,600 --> 00:34:22,800
What interview?

456
00:34:23,679 --> 00:34:24,879
Oh?

457
00:34:24,880 --> 00:34:26,199
Claire didn't tell you?

458
00:34:33,320 --> 00:34:34,439
<i>Okay then.</i>

459
00:34:34,440 --> 00:34:37,600
<i>Since you're here with us today, Ms. Cha,</i>

460
00:34:38,440 --> 00:34:43,279
<i>a lot of people know about
the issues between you and Ms. Claire.</i>

461
00:34:43,280 --> 00:34:46,159
And many already know what caused them.

462
00:34:47,040 --> 00:34:50,000
You mean the fact that
Claire slept with my boyfriend Chris?

463
00:34:56,719 --> 00:34:57,679
It's okay.

464
00:34:57,680 --> 00:35:01,079
Honestly, I'm over that now.

465
00:35:01,080 --> 00:35:02,879
That's a relief.

466
00:35:02,880 --> 00:35:06,479
I thought you two
were still angry with each other.

467
00:35:06,480 --> 00:35:09,039
To tell you the truth, I was angry.

468
00:35:09,040 --> 00:35:13,000
Anyone would be upset
over something like that, right?

469
00:35:13,520 --> 00:35:16,959
<i>But after the crash, I realized that</i>

470
00:35:16,960 --> 00:35:20,719
<i>people should forgive each other
while they still have the chance.</i>

471
00:35:20,720 --> 00:35:22,679
<i>That's really nice to hear.</i>

472
00:35:22,680 --> 00:35:23,559
<i>Then...</i>

473
00:35:23,560 --> 00:35:27,199
<i>But I won't mind if Claire wants
to apologize right now.</i>

474
00:35:27,200 --> 00:35:28,200
Excuse me.

475
00:35:29,080 --> 00:35:30,319
Can we stop the show?

476
00:35:30,320 --> 00:35:31,839
I need to talk to Ms. Claire.

477
00:35:31,840 --> 00:35:33,560
We can't. We're live.

478
00:35:36,040 --> 00:35:37,600
Why not?

479
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:45,239
This is exactly what I came here
to tell everyone today.

480
00:35:45,240 --> 00:35:48,079
And I don't just want to apologize to Cha.

481
00:35:48,080 --> 00:35:50,679
<i>I want to apologize to everyone</i>

482
00:35:50,680 --> 00:35:53,239
<i>for everything I may have done
that upset people.</i>

483
00:35:53,240 --> 00:35:55,799
SOCIALITE'S CONFESSION
AFTER SURVIVING DEATH

484
00:35:55,800 --> 00:35:56,840
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

485
00:36:06,920 --> 00:36:07,959
<i>Claire.</i>

486
00:36:07,960 --> 00:36:10,159
<i>Is this a real apology or just content?</i>

487
00:36:10,160 --> 00:36:11,600
MS. KHAEDARUN OPENS UP
AFTER SURVIVING A NEAR-DEATH EXPERIENCE

488
00:36:13,600 --> 00:36:14,599
<i>It's nothing.</i>

489
00:36:14,600 --> 00:36:16,479
<i>I'm just curious.</i>

490
00:36:16,480 --> 00:36:18,719
<i>Because Claire has actor friends,</i>

491
00:36:18,720 --> 00:36:21,559
<i>so I'm wondering
if she's using acting techniques</i>

492
00:36:21,560 --> 00:36:24,679
<i>she picked up from them in real life.</i>

493
00:36:24,680 --> 00:36:26,080
<i>Is it a real apology?</i>

494
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:30,559
<i>The truth is,</i>

495
00:36:30,560 --> 00:36:33,599
<i>the Claire today
and the Claire from last year</i>

496
00:36:33,600 --> 00:36:34,800
<i>aren't the same person.</i>

497
00:36:36,920 --> 00:36:38,360
What do you mean by that?

498
00:36:39,040 --> 00:36:41,119
<i>The reason I say that is...</i>

499
00:36:41,120 --> 00:36:43,880
<i>I don't remember anything
I did in the past.</i>

500
00:36:44,480 --> 00:36:46,639
<i>It's a result of the helicopter crash.</i>

501
00:36:46,640 --> 00:36:50,199
<i>Everyone sees I look fine and act normal.</i>

502
00:36:50,200 --> 00:36:53,839
<i>But the truth is
I suffered a brain injury.</i>

503
00:36:53,840 --> 00:36:55,879
<i>Some memories are gone.</i>

504
00:36:55,880 --> 00:36:59,359
<i>To put it simply, I have amnesia.</i>

505
00:36:59,360 --> 00:37:02,079
<i>Oh my gosh, I just got chills.</i>

506
00:37:02,080 --> 00:37:05,879
I didn't know until now
that you lost your memories.

507
00:37:05,880 --> 00:37:07,799
<i>Not just memories.</i>

508
00:37:07,800 --> 00:37:09,919
<i>My personality has changed too.</i>

509
00:37:09,920 --> 00:37:15,159
<i>But that's not an excuse to shirk
responsibility for what I did in the past.</i>

510
00:37:15,160 --> 00:37:18,079
<i>That's why I wanted to come on your show.</i>

511
00:37:18,080 --> 00:37:19,800
<i>To apologize to everyone.</i>

512
00:37:23,080 --> 00:37:24,000
<i>Cha.</i>

513
00:37:25,400 --> 00:37:26,560
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

514
00:37:29,360 --> 00:37:32,520
<i>Got anything more sincere than that,
Claire?</i>

515
00:37:33,280 --> 00:37:34,799
<i>Like...</i>

516
00:37:34,800 --> 00:37:38,599
Would you like to kneel at my feet
and apologize to me?

517
00:37:38,600 --> 00:37:41,240
KHAEDARUN'S CONFESSION
AFTER SURVIVING DEATH

518
00:37:46,320 --> 00:37:49,999
How dare your daughter make Claire
bow to her feet and apologize.

519
00:37:50,000 --> 00:37:51,760
Call her and stop her.

520
00:37:53,000 --> 00:37:55,279
But Claire admitted it herself,

521
00:37:55,280 --> 00:37:57,679
that she stole Cha's boyfriend.

522
00:37:57,680 --> 00:38:00,599
The one at fault should apologize, right?

523
00:38:00,600 --> 00:38:01,840
At fault?

524
00:38:02,720 --> 00:38:05,359
The only thing she did wrong
was fight with Cha.

525
00:38:05,360 --> 00:38:07,959
And she already apologized
to put this behind them!

526
00:38:07,960 --> 00:38:10,999
Do you need to see her sleeping
with Cha's boyfriend

527
00:38:11,000 --> 00:38:13,319
to realize that your granddaughter
is a slut?

528
00:38:13,320 --> 00:38:14,720
Rossarin!

529
00:38:20,600 --> 00:38:21,880
I don't think so.

530
00:38:25,280 --> 00:38:29,040
I think someone
is trying to frame Ms. Claire.

531
00:38:44,880 --> 00:38:46,280
What's going on?

532
00:38:49,400 --> 00:38:51,600
I think we should stop here for today.

533
00:38:52,760 --> 00:38:54,040
Wait.

534
00:38:55,040 --> 00:38:58,040
You said someone framed Claire.

535
00:38:59,600 --> 00:39:00,720
What about this video?

536
00:39:11,360 --> 00:39:14,680
Are you still accusing me
of framing Claire?

537
00:39:17,920 --> 00:39:18,840
Claire.

538
00:39:20,040 --> 00:39:22,200
Why must you take everything from me?

539
00:39:27,640 --> 00:39:28,680
I...

540
00:39:29,640 --> 00:39:30,759
Sir, you can't come in.

541
00:39:30,760 --> 00:39:33,160
You can't come in, sir. You can't come in.

542
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:36,640
These flowers are for Ms. Claire.

543
00:39:39,800 --> 00:39:42,119
Well, she's allergic to pollen.

544
00:39:42,120 --> 00:39:43,839
I'm her fiancé.

545
00:39:43,840 --> 00:39:45,320
I'll take them on her behalf.

546
00:39:54,920 --> 00:39:56,279
Claire.

547
00:39:56,280 --> 00:39:57,200
What are you doing?

548
00:39:57,920 --> 00:39:59,240
We can talk this out.

549
00:39:59,880 --> 00:40:01,119
Talk?

550
00:40:01,120 --> 00:40:04,680
I guess you don't know my sister is dead.

551
00:40:05,520 --> 00:40:06,760
Mina.

552
00:40:07,400 --> 00:40:09,039
The employee that you...

553
00:40:09,040 --> 00:40:10,800
treated like an animal!

554
00:40:11,560 --> 00:40:12,639
Do you remember her?!

555
00:40:12,640 --> 00:40:15,959
<i>You're so stupid.
How can anyone be this stupid?</i>

556
00:40:15,960 --> 00:40:17,719
I'm Mina's mother.

557
00:40:17,720 --> 00:40:19,959
It's all your fault! Why did you hurt her?

558
00:40:19,960 --> 00:40:22,320
Why did you hurt her? Why?!

559
00:40:23,240 --> 00:40:25,719
You... you're Mina's brother?

560
00:40:25,720 --> 00:40:27,520
Please calm down.

561
00:40:28,320 --> 00:40:30,039
Let's talk this through.

562
00:40:30,040 --> 00:40:32,240
We'll take responsibility, okay?

563
00:40:32,920 --> 00:40:34,080
Take responsibility?

564
00:40:34,800 --> 00:40:35,880
How?!

565
00:40:36,600 --> 00:40:37,840
My sister is dead!

566
00:40:39,040 --> 00:40:40,280
And my mother...

567
00:40:40,840 --> 00:40:42,840
She's dying too.

568
00:40:45,720 --> 00:40:48,240
Because of her. Because of her!

569
00:41:10,720 --> 00:41:13,319
Kneel at Claire's feet
and apologize to her.

570
00:41:13,320 --> 00:41:15,999
<i>If Nitchan can prove he's truly capable,</i>

571
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:17,880
I'll give him a chance.

572
00:41:19,320 --> 00:41:21,399
<i>Do you remember what you did?</i>

573
00:41:21,400 --> 00:41:23,319
<i>Chan never told you about it?</i>

574
00:41:23,320 --> 00:41:25,479
What if I never get my memory back?

575
00:41:25,480 --> 00:41:26,960
<i>What...</i>

576
00:41:27,560 --> 00:41:29,240
<i>did you say to the chairman?</i>

577
00:41:29,840 --> 00:41:30,599
Sir.

578
00:41:30,600 --> 00:41:32,519
What did you and Claire
talk about last night?

579
00:41:32,520 --> 00:41:34,679
She sent me a message last night.

580
00:41:34,680 --> 00:41:36,560
Claire? Claire!
